        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3c8336ae-f628-5a35-be6b-b6891fda233a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Carpentaria acuminata, Carpentaria, Panax, ginseng\n- Taxonomy: Araliaceae\n- Places: Northern Territory, Australia, Gulf of Carpentaria, Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System\n- Ecosystems: tidal wetlands\n\nFacts:\n- Carpentaria acuminata, also called the carpentaria palm, is the only species in the genus Carpentaria.\n- Carpentaria acuminata is native to tropical coastal regions in the north of the Northern Territory, Australia.\n- Panax, also called ginseng, belongs to the Araliaceae family.\n- The Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System comprises a 994 km tract of tidal wetlands on the south-west coast of the Gulf of Carpentaria in the Northern Territory of Australia.",
